{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 5xx up to 71.8%) are caused by slow inventory POST /reserve, which began right after inventory was deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.1 at 07:18:17Z. Orders times out waiting on inventory and returns 504, and gateway turns that into 502. Inventory itself returns no 5xx, but its p95 latency rose to 4.77s and it holds most of the self time in failing traces.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory release 3.2.1, deployed at 07:18:17Z, made POST /reserve slow (self time ~2.4-2.6s, p95 up to 4.77s). This exceeds the orders timeout, so orders returns 504 and gateway fails checkout with 502. The deploy is linked to the symptoms by timing: first errors appear about 2s after it (07:18:19Z). Release tags also match: all failing traces carry inventory=3.2.1. What the code change in 3.2.1 actually was is not in the evidence.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "high",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-190058c637be",
   "ev-5fa58511a1e2",
   "ev-51525d7035d0",
   "ev-676b84478541"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders reports inventory reservation timeouts as 504s, which propagate to gateway as 502s. Inventory shows 0% 5xx because it is slow, not failing.",
